.TH "PB-CONFIG-CUSTOMIZE-SHOW" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-customize-show - Show the local preference document


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config customize show [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the local preference document

.PP
Show the effective local preference document, including current shortcuts and appearance settings. The command does not execute any customized command.

.PP
Customization is local to this CLI installation. It can change shortcuts, command defaults, and terminal appearance without changing account credentials or remote resources. Validate or explain preferences before applying an unfamiliar document.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for show

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config-customize(1)\fP
